unofficial-ercot-mms-skin
Copyright 2026 Wattness

This project is an independent, unofficial recreation of the visual style of
the Market Management System (MMS) screens operated by the Electric
Reliability Council of Texas, Inc. (ERCOT). It is not ERCOT software and is
not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by ERCOT. The name "ERCOT" is
used only to describe what the style recreates; ERCOT's names and marks belong
to ERCOT.

Third-party material

docs/ercot/ holds excerpts from documents ERCOT published on www.ercot.com,
and the text of ERCOT's Website User Agreement. They are ERCOT's and are not
covered by this project's MIT licence. They are not part of the npm package.

  - One image is a file ERCOT published inside its presentation
    ERCOT-TWG-2026-08-20-NPRR-1188-System-Impacts.pptx (ppt/media/image11.png),
    kept byte for byte, with ERCOT's Website User Agreement beside it in
    docs/ercot/ERCOT-TERMS-OF-USE.txt.
  - Eight images are crops of screenshots and of rendered pages from ERCOT's
    2007 documents on the design of these screens. Each is credited to its
    source where it is shown. They compare the skin with ERCOT's published
    designs and record how those designs were reviewed. Section 5 of the
    Agreement covers unmodified contents only; it does not cover these
    crops, and no permission from ERCOT is claimed for them.

docs/sources.md lists each file with its source document, URL and SHA-256, how
it was made, and how it relates to the Agreement. None shows an ERCOT logo.
Apart from the Agreement's text, no whole ERCOT document is included, and no
ERCOT logo, schema, code or font. docs/provenance.md and docs/sources.md also
quote short passages from ERCOT documents and web pages, each credited to its
source.

Ten values in src/tokens.css were measured from the first image:

  ERCOT-TWG-2026-08-20-NPRR-1188-System-Impacts.pptx, ppt/media/image11.png
  https://www.ercot.com/files/docs/2026/08/20/ERCOT-TWG-2026-08-20-NPRR-1188-System-Impacts.pptx

scripts/verify-provenance.mjs downloads that file when run, to check the
values, and does not store or redistribute it.

Fonts

No font files are bundled. The stylesheet names fonts installed with common
operating systems (Verdana, Tahoma, Geneva, Georgia, Menlo, Consolas) and
generic CSS families (ui-monospace, monospace, sans-serif, serif). Fonts are
loaded from the user's system under their owners' licences.
